<h2 id="why-denver">Why side hustles in Denver pay off</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>High incomes, busy schedules.</strong> Denver has a large base of well-paid professionals in tech, aerospace, healthcare and energy, from Lockheed Martin and Ball Corp to Denver Health, UCHealth and DaVita. They would rather ski on Saturday than clean gutters, and they pay for help.</li>
  <li><strong>A packed venue calendar.</strong> Broncos games at Empower Field at Mile High, Nuggets and Avalanche at Ball Arena, Rockies at Coors Field, plus Red Rocks Amphitheatre in Morrison from spring through fall. The National Western Stock Show in January and the Great American Beer Festival in the fall bring waves of visitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Wild weather swings.</strong> Spring snowstorms, summer hail and a long, dry fire season mean snow removal, hail cleanup and yard work arrive in bursts. Being ready when the forecast turns is half the business.</li>
  <li><strong>An outdoor economy.</strong> Bikes, skis, dogs and trail days are a way of life here, which creates demand you won't find in most cities.</li>
</ul>

